  "answer": "Not all checks pass. The build passed, but the unit tests failed, and the component stage was skipped because the run stopped at the failure.\n\n| Stage | Result |\n|---|---|\n| build (`make build`) | passed |\n| unit (`make unit`) | **failed**, exit code 2 |\n| component (`make component`) | skipped |\n\n**Unit tests:** 272 total, 233 passed, 39 failed. The log has two runs (net9.0 and net10.0), so the failures show up twice in it. The 39 are unique tests, and all fail from one cause.\n\n**Cause:** every built-in semantic matcher is rejected as unknown. Here are two of the errors:\n```\nSystem.ArgumentException : Unknown semantic matcher 'isuuid' for field 'id'\nSystem.ArgumentException : Unknown semantic matcher 'isnull' for field 'deletedAt'\n```\n`SemanticMatcher.ParseSpec` lowercases every matcher name (`src/ConfIT/Matching/SemanticMatcher.cs:85` and `:91`). The `BuiltIns` dictionary at `:8-22` is case-sensitive and has camelCase keys such as `isUuid` and `greaterThan`. The lookup at `:59` can therefore never match, and it throws at `:61`.\n\n**Affected tests:**\n- **`SemanticMatcherTests`:** 34 tests, with the same error for `isUuid`, `isNull`, `isNotNull`, `isEmail`, `isIsoDateTime`, `isNotEmpty`, `greaterThan` and `lessThan`.\n- **`ResultMatcherTests`:** 5 tests. One example is `MatchResponseBody_NullExpectedWithSemanticMatcher_DoesNotThrow`, which reports `Did not expect any exception, but found System.ArgumentException: Unknown semantic matcher 'isuuid' for field 'id'`.\n- **`Apply_FieldAbsentFromResponse_ThrowsInvalidOperationException`:** it expects an `InvalidOperationException`. The unknown-matcher `ArgumentException` fires before the field-absent check, so it gets that instead.\n\nI didn't modify any files.",
